"t": "Section A5. Section A5. Say each of these with any object you like."
},
{
"s": 13.78,
"e": 17.72,
"t": "Shall I use cup? The cup is on the table."
},
{
"s": 18.28,
"e": 22.74,
"t": "Cup, table, mathe aaye. Mathe is on top of or on."
},
{
"s": 24.16,
"e": 26.04,
"t": "Would we say that? We wouldn't say cup, table, aye?"
},
{
"s": 26.47,
"e": 29.31,
"t": "No. Cup, table, mathe aaye."
},
{
"s": 30.85,
"e": 31.79,
"t": "Doesn't that mean it's above the table?"
},
{
"s": 35.01,
"e": 37.79,
"t": "It means above. It means on top of. It means both."
},
{
"s": 38.27,
"e": 40.89,
"t": "How would you say dinner's on the table or food's on the table?"
},
{
"s": 41.41,
"e": 42.53,
"t": "Kenjo table mathe aaye."
},
{
"s": 45.43,
"e": 47.49,
