},
{
"s": 49.15,
"e": 53.61,
"t": "Actually, coming back to the cup, you could also say cup, table, je mathe aaye."
},
{
"s": 56.56,
"e": 59.74,
"t": "Maybe je, there is a bit like the, is on top of the table."
},
{
"s": 60.06,
"e": 62.2,
"t": "That sounds more like what I'm familiar with, no?"
},
{
"s": 62.8,
"e": 67.64,
"t": "Yeah. Cup, table, mathe aaye, is more colloquial, is more everyday word."
},
{
"s": 67.98,
"e": 71.24,
"t": "Table, je mathe aaye is more a fuller version of it."
},
{
"s": 72.02,
"e": 74.18,
"t": "So what was the next one? Under the table?"
},
{
"s": 74.88,
"e": 76.22,
"t": "Cup, table, je niche aaye."
},
{
"s": 77.94,
"e": 80.58,
"t": "So that's under, underneath, beneath, niche."
},
{
"s": 82.98,
"e": 92.36,
"t": "In the cupboard would be andar. Cup, table, cup, kabat je andar aaye. Kabat being cupboard."
},
{
"s": 94.72,
"e": 100.44,
"t": "And andar, not under, andar is underneath, sorry inside."
},
{
"s": 101.34,
"e": 110.62,
"t": "So space relation belongs to the object. It's in the table's underside. It's on the table's top side."
},
{
"s": 111.1,
"e": 125.1,
"t": "It's in the table's nearby side. So say cup, kabat je andar aaye. Cup, cupboards, inside is something like that?"
},
{
"s": 127.2,
"e": 136.06,
"t": "Yeah. Kabat je andar aaye. Kabat je is like belonging to the cupboard."
},
{
"s": 136.32,
"e": 139.92,
"t": "So kabat je andar is saying under the inside that belongs to the cupboard."
},
{
"s": 139.92,
"e": 141.72,
"t": "Yeah, that's where the cup is."
},
{
"s": 141.86,
"e": 145.78,
"t": "That's what the cup is. Yeah, exactly. That's what you're saying."
},
{
"s": 146.7,
"e": 149.18,
"t": "The key is behind the door."
},
{
"s": 150.72,
"e": 157.32,
"t": "Chawi darwaje je putiya aaye. Chawi is key. Darwaje is again relation to the door."
},
{
"s": 158.26,
"e": 160.7,
"t": "Putiya is behind. Aye is is."
},
{
"s": 161.14,
"e": 163.24,
"t": "A darwajo is the door. Darwajo is the door."
},
{
"s": 163.82,
"e": 166.84,
"t": "So chawi darwaje je putiya aaye."
},
{
"s": 169.16,
"e": 170.5,
"t": "Next to the plate."
},
{
"s": 171.94,
"e": 176.7,
"t": "Sani je baju me. Sani is plate. Baju me is nearby."
},
{
"s": 178.32,
"e": 180.32,
"t": "In front of Nana."
},
{
"s": 181.0,
"e": 188.58,
"t": "In front of is agiya. If you want to say in front of it, inje agiya. Or in front of the cup, cup je agiya."
},
{
"s": 190.4,
"e": 192.86,
"t": "So how would you say put it in front of? In front of the plate."
},
{
"s": 193.28,
"e": 196.98,
"t": "Sani je agiya rak. Rak is put."
},
{
"s": 197.76,
"e": 198.44,
"t": "Sane? What's sane?"
},
{
"s": 201.66,
"e": 203.22,
"t": "Sane is opposite."
},
{
"s": 204.74,
"e": 206.78,
"t": "One's in front, one's opposite. Which one's which?"
},
{
"s": 208.26,
"e": 216.96,
"t": "Agiya is in front. Sane is, so like if you were sitting, I would say munje sane rak. That means put it across in front of me so I can see it."
},
{
"s": 216.96,
"e": 223.82,
"t": "So say you were moving the laptop and I'd say put it in front of me, munje sane rak. So sane is almost making it face me."
},
{
"s": 224.42,
"e": 236.54,
"t": "It's opposite. Yeah, but particularly it means... Opposite but facing. Yeah, agiya would just mean anywhere in front of me."
},
{
"s": 236.96,
"e": 240.8,
"t": "Sane means particularly in front of me but like facing me, right ahead of me."
},
{
"s": 240.8,
"e": 246.44,
"t": "So if you said, if you were telling someone to sit opposite..."
},
{
"s": 246.44,
"e": 248.82,
"t": "Yeah, you would say munje sane we."
},
{
"s": 249.5,
"e": 252.66,
"t": "We being sit. Munje is me."
},
{
"s": 253.98,
"e": 256.56,
"t": "Was your. Munje sane we."
},
{
"s": 257.46,
"e": 263.08,
"t": "In my, in front of space, sit. Munjo belonging to me, sane."
},
{
"s": 264.2,
"e": 270.12,
"t": "The space that is, the attribute which belongs to being opposite me, occupy that."
},
{
"s": 270.38,
"e": 272.9,
"t": "Munje agiya jagai ida we."
},
{
"s": 274.02,
"e": 279.06,
"t": "Munje agiya is in front of me. Jagai is space. I is is."
},
{
"s": 279.4,
"e": 289.8,
"t": "Ida we sit there. So yeah, if you formally spread it out, you are describing the space as it belongs to you and then placing that person in that space. Yeah, that's right."
},
